feat(run): request minimal drain on the accurate leg when not verifying

Pass --drain-minimal to the vsim accurate leg unless --verify is set, so an
unverified hybrid run skips the full register-file drain it never reads (only
the mcycle delta feeds the window-cycles figure). The policy sits at the plan's
Step-construction site next to the rest of the verify reasoning, not in
vsim_extra_args (which is scoped to user-forwarded, trigger-validated flags).
USER_GUIDE notes the trade-off: --verify keeps the full, slower drain.

